      <article class="paper featured reveal">
        <div>
          <div class="venue-badge">ICLR 2027 · Under review</div>
          <div class="venue"><span class="pill">First author</span></div>
          <h3>EKLAV: Elicited Key CoT Learning via Answer-Only Supervision</h3>
          <p class="formerly">Formerly released as TabRank.</p>
          <dl class="steps">
            <div><dt>Problem</dt><dd>Small AI models are expensive to train when they copy a large model's full reasoning.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Idea</dt><dd>Show the reasoning in the prompt, and train the small model only on the final answer.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Result</dt><dd>Better ranking on 41 of 48 tests, with up to 32% less training compute.</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="explain">BRIGHT is a benchmark that tests how well a model ranks documents for a question, across 12 subject areas.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="side">
          <div class="facts">
            <div class="fact">
              <div class="num"><span class="grad-text">41 of 48</span></div>
              <div class="cap">ranking tests won on BRIGHT</div>
            </div>
            <div class="fact">
              <div class="num"><span class="grad-text">29</span> models</div>
              <div class="cap">and 7 datasets released on Hugging Face</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="links">
            <a class="link arxiv" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25182" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img class="ico" src="/icons/arxiv.svg" alt="" width="16" height="16" />Read on arXiv</a>
            <a class="link" href="https://huggingface.co/AdarshSingh7647" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img class="ico" src="/icons/huggingface.svg" alt="" width="16" height="16" />Models on Hugging Face</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="paper reveal">
        <div>
          <div class="venue-badge">ACL 2026 · Main conference</div>
          <div class="venue"><span class="pill">First author</span></div>
          <h3>CRAFT: Training-Free Cascaded Retrieval for Tabular QA</h3>
          <dl class="steps">
            <div><dt>Problem</dt><dd>Finding the right table for a question means checking many tables. That is slow.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Idea</dt><dd>A cheap filter removes most tables first. A stronger model then ranks the rest. No training needed.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Result</dt><dd>The right table is in the top 10 results for 87.16% of questions.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <div class="side">
          <div class="facts">
            <div class="fact">
              <div class="num"><span class="grad-text">87.16%</span></div>
              <div class="cap">top 10 recall on NQ-Tables</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="links">
            <a class="link acl" href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.acl-long.149/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img class="ico" src="/icons/acl.svg" alt="" width="16" height="16" />ACL Anthology</a>
            <a class="link arxiv" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.14984" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img class="ico" src="/icons/arxiv.svg" alt="" width="16" height="16" />arXiv</a>
            <a class="link gh" href="https://github.com/coral-lab-asu/CRAFT" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img class="ico" src="/icons/github.svg" alt="" width="16" height="16" />Code</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

